<title>SPAIN: Spain's Catalonia to auction 3-, 5-, 10-year bonds.</title>
<headline>Spain's Catalonia to auction 3-, 5-, 10-year bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Catalonia regional government said on Friday it would auction three-, five-, and 10-year bonds for a total of 10 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>The auction will be on July 10 with payment on July 17.</p>
<p> ISSUE			    COUPON	EXPECTED AMOUNT</p>
<p> 3 yr Bono 12/04/2000	 5.30 pct    3 billion pesetas</p>
<p> 5 yr Bono 27/02/2002	 5.75 pct    3 billion pesetas</p>
<p>10 yr Bono 28/03/2007	 6.70 pct    4 billion pesetas</p>
<p>NOTE - All these bonds are new tranches of previous issues already auctioned on June 12 when Catalonia reopened its monthly note and bond auction.</p>
<p>Following are the results of the June 12 auction (amount in billion pesetas):</p>
<p>    ISSUE	 YIELDS    PRICES	  BID	    ALLOTTED</p>
<p>    5.30%-2000  5.248     101.1	   13.5	     2.5</p>
<p>    5.75%-2002  5.708     101.9	   15.8	     3.0</p>
<p>    6.70%-2007  6.613     102.1	   21.3	     4.5</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
